From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 20:24:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] phy: allwinner: Add a driver for the A733 PCIe combo PHY

The second combo PHY (COMB1) of the A733 carries the single lane of the
PCIe controller. Without it the controller has no link to train.

Add a driver for its PCIe function. It selects PCIe in the protocol mux,
takes the PLL reference from the oscillator, programs the PMA, releases
the PHY and its lane from reset, waits for the PMA common block with a
timeout and enables the reference clock output once the PHY is ready,
as the manual recommends. Exit turns that output off again before it
puts the PHY back into reset.

The wrapper registers follow the A733 user manual (V1.00, 18.2.6). The
PMA registers are not documented; their values are those of the vendor
kernel, and those that the first combo PHY writes with the same value
for USB3 are shared settings. The difference from the vendor code: the
PHY does not open the bus gates of the PCIe controller, which the
controller claims itself; the reference clock gate is a clock of the
SERDES CCU instead of a register write; the wait for the PMA times out
instead of spinning forever; and a vendor read-modify-write whose
result is overwritten by a constant is reduced to that constant.

The protocol mux sits in the SERDES top page, shared with the first
combo PHY; the driver reaches it through the syscon regmap.

Not covered: COMB1 in its USB3 role, and L1 substates.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on one board; the COMB1 PHY bound, set
its lane to PCIe through the SERDES top syscon and powered up, and its
PMA reported ready; exit did not run.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/phy/allwinner/Kconfig                 |  15 +
 drivers/phy/allwinner/Makefile                |   1 +
 .../allwinner/phy-sun60i-a733-pcie-combophy.c | 405 ++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 421 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun60i-a733-pcie-combophy.c

diff --git a/drivers/phy/allwinner/Kconfig b/drivers/phy/allwinner/Kconfig
index e6342c8880cd..4676270711c6 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/allwinner/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/phy/allwinner/Kconfig
@@ -88,3 +88,18 @@ config PHY_SUN60I_A733_COMBO
 	  the orientation switch for it. DisplayPort is not supported.
 
 	  If unsure and building for an A733, say M.
+
+config PHY_SUN60I_A733_PCIE_COMBO
+	tristate "Allwinner A733 PCIe combo PHY driver"
+	depends on ARCH_SUNXI || COMPILE_TEST
+	depends on HAS_IOMEM && OF
+	depends on RESET_CONTROLLER
+	select GENERIC_PHY
+	select MFD_SYSCON
